<metadata><name>East Lake</name><desc>or-central-meissner-1984:61: route read from the book's text and sketch map. One trkseg per waypoint pair, in order; segment sources are in the trk desc. Geometry from OSM (ODbL, (c) OpenStreetMap contributors) and USFS EDW (public domain) where marked; 'straight' segments are off-trail connectors, not traced.</desc></metadata>
<wpt lat="43.712347" lon="-121.277964"><ele>1934.6</ele><name>Paulina Lake, across from the road to Paulina Lake Lodge</name><desc>source: DB trailhead pin th:paulina-lake-lodge (OSM node 38373784, junction of road 21, NF 500 and the lodge spur); reached in winter by skiing tour 58 from Ten Mile Sno-Park; confidence: high; pdf_page: 121; book_elev_ft: 6331; quote: Follow directions to Paulina Lake. From there stay on the main road #21.</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="43.712302" lon="-121.277653"><ele>1935.2</ele><name>Road 21 east of the junction</name><desc>source: OSM node 38307726, west end of way 5378046 (Forest Service Road 21), 25 m east of the pin across the unnamed tertiary way 5361299; confidence: high; pdf_page: 121; quote: From there stay on the main road #21.</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="43.718453" lon="-121.201255"><ele>1957.3</ele><name>Hot Springs Campground (road 21 beside it)</name><desc>source: OSM node 38580027 on NF 21 (way 5375402), nearest to OSM Hot Springs Campground (node 3620983697), 124 m away; map 64 circle 2; confidence: medium; pdf_page: 121; quote: It is about five miles to East Lake. ... At East Lake the area of the hot springs makes a good destination</desc></wpt>
<trk><name>East Lake</name><desc>1. Paulina Lake, across from the road to Paulina Lake Lodge -&gt; Road 21 east of the junction: osm (high), 0.02 mi | 2. Road 21 east of the junction -&gt; Hot Springs Campground (road 21 beside it): osm (high), 4.43 mi</desc>
